{
  "id": "COMPOUND:10898 - PROTEIN:6153",
  "verbalization": "Tucaresol is implicated in the regulation of Lysine-specific demethylase 4D-like through a multi-step mechanism involving dehydrogenase/reductase SDR family member 9. This pathway is supported by multiple evidence chains, each linking Tucaresol to a different compound that targets the same enzyme. The first evidence chain connects Tucaresol directly to dehydrogenase/reductase SDR family member 9, which in turn is targeted by 5alpha,6alpha-Epoxy(22e,24r)-ergosta-8(14),22-dien-3beta,7alpha-diol, a compound that also targets Lysine-specific demethylase 4D-like. The second evidence chain provides an additional layer of support, showing that Dendridine A, another compound targeting SDR family member 9, also influences Lysine-specific demethylase 4D-like. The third evidence chain further strengthens this relationship by showing that a more complex compound, (6aR,9R)-N-...-carboxamide, also targets Lysine-specific demethylase 4D-like through the same intermediate. These findings collectively suggest that Tucaresol may modulate Lysine-specific demethylase 4D-like through the dehydrogenase/reductase SDR family member 9 pathway, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be fully elucidated. The evidence supports a direct, mechanistic link between Tucaresol and Lysine-specific demethylase 4D-like, with the observed scores indicating a plausible biological relationship.",
